{
  "abstract": "Let $H$ be the lift of one modular hyperbola $(x+A)(y+B)\\equiv c\\pmod p$ to a square window of side $n=\\theta p$ with $3\\le\\theta<4$, at an arbitrary translation. We show that every subset of $H$ with no three points collinear has at most $\\big(\\tfrac32-\\tfrac{9\\min(4-\\theta,1/3)^2}{16\\theta}\\big)n+O(\\sqrt p\\log^2p)$ points. Together with earlier rStation results at sides $2p$ to $3p$, $3p$ and $4p$, one hyperbola has density at most $3/2+o(1)$ in every square window of side between $2p$ and $4p$. The previous uniform bound on $[3p,4p]$ was about $1.511$. Arguments confined to reciprocal orbits $\\{u,-c/u,-u,c/u\\}$ cannot give this: with all lines inside orbits, the bound exceeds $3/2$ at worst translations for $\\theta$ between $11/3$ and $4$ (computed). The new ingredient couples the orbit of $u$ to the orbit of $2u$, the pairs joined by the slopes $\\pm2$ and $\\pm\\tfrac12$. These pairs form a 2-regular graph on orbits, so half the sum of pair capacities bounds $|S|$, and a Kloosterman-sum estimate reduces that sum to a torus integral. We evaluate the integral exactly. The phase space splits into 13,888 rational polytopes. On each, the integral is an explicit quadratic, which we maximise exactly, and the polytopes are complete by exact volume. For $\\theta\\ge11/3$ the maximum is attained at the translation $A/p=B/p=(4-\\theta)/2$, so the bound is sharp for the relaxation and its margin closes quadratically as $\\theta\\to4$. The result is computed and conditional. It depends on the capacities of 0/1 programs with at most 128 variables, solved by HiGHS at zero gap. An independent CaDiCaL UNSAT check, still incomplete, has confirmed the first 898 capacities with no errors. Above $4p$ the same relaxation allows $1.5107$ at $\\theta=4.1$, and we give no construction.",
